  "configuration_id": "config_005",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_002 (rna_only, multiprofile, pca_n2000, avgpool) is the current best at 0.591 acc, showing multiprofile+avgpool is the strongest RNA configuration. Image (resnet50) is very weak (0.208), so the RNA representation is the dominant lever. Uncertainty: we don't yet know whether a learned RNA encoder (scvi_n200) would improve over linear PCA in this best-known setting. This experiment (config_005) changes only the RNA encoder from pca_n2000 to scvi_n200 while holding multiprofile+avgpool fixed, giving a clean single-variable comparison against config_002. If scvi helps, it opens a new improvement axis before investing in multimodal fusion; if it doesn't, PCA is confirmed sufficient and we can redirect budget toward image encoder quality or fusion strategy. Under a limited budget, resolving whether representation learning matters is the highest-information next step."
}

